turnip: darwin, in a sysmem pass a draw that reads the attachments it renders to waits for the earlier draws' writes

Metal's framebuffer fetch reaches Turnip as input attachments that are also colour attachments of the subpass (metal2vulkan's
lowering: SubpassData reads in the fragment shader). Core Animation uses it for glass, backdrop and vibrancy layers (the host trace of
2026-11-12: an SDF written into a memoryless colour attachment, then read by the glass draw of the same pass), and RenderBox for
clips, blend modes and shadows, since the device answers MTLGPUFamilyApple1-3, which have programmable blending. metal2vulkan declares
the colour attachments as input attachments of every subpass and puts the colour feedback-loop and rasterization-order flags on every
pipeline; the feedback-loop flag disables GMEM (rp.disable_gmem), so these passes render in sysmem whatever TU_DEBUG says. There the
fragment shader reads the image through UCHE while the earlier draws' pixels may still be in the CCU, and only SINGLE_PRIM_MODE
(FLUSH_PER_OVERLAP_AND_OVERWRITE) keeps the two in step: a6xx's mechanism, never checked on the A830.

Before each draw whose fragment shader reads an input attachment (one with non-bindless texture slots, ir3's num_samp: input
attachments are the only descriptors that take them; or a dynamic pass's dynamic_input_attachments_used), a sysmem pass now cleans
the CCU (colour and depth), invalidates UCHE, cleans the blit cache and waits for the writes and for idle, under CP_COND_REG_EXEC on
the render mode, so GMEM passes and the binning pass skip it. In the host trace that was 1 draw in 30 for Core Animation's glass frame
and 6 in 38 for RenderBox's clip, blend-mode and shadow shapes. The first such draw of a process says so once: "TU: info: draws that
read the attachments they render to (first: <what made it one>): in a sysmem pass each waits ...". TU_DEBUG=nofbflush leaves it out
(the A/B against 0001-0006); TU_DEBUG=fbflushall also flushes before every draw of a feedback-loop subpass or rasterization-order
pipeline (every draw of these passes). Against the tree after 0001-0006. MIT, as the files.

